cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize this dataset, system design, or paper in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "An IoT-Based Infrastructure Model for Reducing Urban Light Pollution: Empirical Assessment and System Design in Dhaka"
abstract: >-
  This repository provides an empirical baseline of urban light pollution in Dhaka,
  Bangladesh, comprising 220 in-situ photometric measurements across 13 functional urban
  sectors alongside 12 controlled benchtop luminaire experiments. To eliminate continuous
  nocturnal over-illumination without compromising public safety, an autonomous, decentralized
  IoT smart streetlight infrastructure is developed. The system features a vertically stratified
  four-zone node architecture managed by an ESP32-S3 Sense microcontroller fusing seven sensing
  modalities (TinyML edge vision, microwave Doppler radar, PIR array, BH1750 ambient light sensor,
  BME280 weather module, DS3231 RTC, and INA219 power telemetry). Nodes broadcast target velocity
  and heading via sub-10 ms OSI Layer-2 ESP-NOW frames to project an illuminated look-ahead safety
  bubble 30-40 m ahead of approaching vehicles while maintaining a 10% eco-baseline across vacant
  roadway segments.
